mods: _vfxprobe
timeout: 120s
hide: false
# The VFX probe (2026-10-22): can a data mod define a NEW particle system with its own art, and re-point a vanilla one?
# No _autoplay: the fight waits on the player's turn, so the probe units stay alive and still while their auras emit.
# Shots: a settled baseline (no probe unit), the NEW system (VfxProbeAura: a Rat with EliteParticle VfxProbeAura, our
# #ff0090 VfxProbeDot clip) three times 25 frames apart, then the re-pointed vanilla system (VfxProbeRepoint: a Rat with
# EliteParticle SparkleBuff, whose movieclip our particles.gon.merge sets to VfxProbeMarker) three times.
# OBSERVED 2026-10-22 (run 20261022-130301): the window capture lands up to ~1 s AFTER the shot event (the baseline
# already showed the aura spawned 700 ms later; the last two shots were lost to the quit) — so every state change waits
# 240 frames after the shot before it, and the script idles 240 frames before quitting.
# editor/scripts/art-probe.ts --vfx reads them (probe-vfx.ts): pink / marker pixels in the arena per shot, how much the
# pink set moves between shots (particles, not a sprite), and it refuses a verdict when the shots are byte-identical.
wait frames 120
seed 42
enter TacticsTest
wait frames 300
shot "baseline"
wait frames 240
cmd spawn VfxProbeAura
expect console "Spawned VfxProbeAura" within 10
wait frames 90
shot "aura 1"
wait frames 25
shot "aura 2"
wait frames 25
shot "aura 3"
wait frames 240
cmd spawn VfxProbeRepoint
expect console "Spawned VfxProbeRepoint" within 10
wait frames 90
shot "repoint 1"
wait frames 25
shot "repoint 2"
wait frames 25
shot "repoint 3"
wait frames 240
quit
